{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner schedule for e3d5a73e (R7 and finding 3.4 cohort). This is a scheduling disposition, not an approval of the plan.\n\n1. Versions: register 19, directory 18, rules 11 and destination 14. Membership 8 and inbox 1 stay. Use these numbers in place of the prospective constants. If the Source work shows that membership or inbox must change too, report it before the head goes to review; do not allocate another number silently. Register 19 is needed because DIRECTORY_OF binds each register version to one directory version.\n\n2. New creation: only dap-demo founds rooms for visitors, so only dap-demo changes its default. After the R7 head lands, the planner founds one new open register at register 19 on dap-demo. One small reviewed config head then points DEMO_START_CONFIG at it. artroom-scope, dap-lending and dap-grow change no default and found nothing new. Their existing scopes stay on their pins.\n\n3. Grow: the grow room stays on the register 17 cohort (directory 16, membership 8, rules 10, destination 12) through the archive work. A move of Grow to the new cohort needs its own request after the archive reaches its cutoff milestone. It is not part of R7.\n\n4. Rollout owner: the planner, after checker review of the exact head. Order:\n   a. The next dap-demo deploy from Main carries R6. It sets PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS to the register 17 cohort, so the existing open register keeps founding rooms. This makes one register change on dap-demo, not two.\n   b. After R7 lands: deploy, found the register 19 open register, land the config head, deploy again, then remove the register 17 allowance from dap-demo.\n   c. The other Workers take the R7 code with their next deploy, with no default change.\n\n5. Live pins, as read back in 99d86feb (22 October) and at the dap-demo founding (23 October). These are readbacks of settings and of operator inspect at those dates, not a scan of every scope:\n   - dap-grow: register 17; room grow-demo directory 16